{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`. The obligations are: (a) no prompt, tool result or tool error states a line number or range of a project source; (b) exceptions for quoted source text and for tool errors that repeat a number the model supplied; (c) source locations are given as file plus outline selector. The selector grammar in `requirements.references.outline_selectors` is only cited context.\n\n**Tool errors**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply]` is an end-to-end test.\n  - A habeas read of a file with a syntax error produces an internal error naming its line. The test asserts that this text is present internally.\n  - The model-bound request, captured through `ReadingProvider`, still says \"cannot parse\" but no longer matches the line-position pattern.\n  - A read starting past the end of the file is asserted to report only the start number the model supplied. This is the exception for repeating a supplied number.\n- `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` checks `without_source_lines` directly on each diagnostic form:\n  - parse errors that name a line;\n  - the supplied single-line and range forms, which are kept verbatim;\n  - `file:N: ` style diagnostics, which become `file#: `;\n  - a second location inside a message (a \"first declared at\" path), which becomes `path#`;\n  - YAML and TOML \"at line, column\" positions, which are stripped.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues]` runs several failing reads through the same sanitizer.\n\n**Tool results**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms]` and `fn[line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes]` assert that habeas results and recorded inputs carry no `line_start` or `line_end`. They identify nodes by selector, and plain-text lines by `line@…`.\n- `fn[search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules]` and `fn[separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line]` assert that ripgrep entries and lines carry no line numbers. The latter compares exact JSON.\n- `fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` asserts exact selector-only outline output.\n- `fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` asserts exact reference sites as file plus item.\n- ast_grep results use the same entry builder (`SearchNodes::entries`) as ripgrep. Their selector-only form is checked in the cargo-output test through `found(&structural)`, which asserts `file#selector` strings.\n\n**Prompts**\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` asserts exact mandatory-input JSON of `file`, `item`, `hash`, `kind` and `text`, with no line numbers.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts that the match payload the model receives (`matches_value`) is exactly `{kind, query, item[, text]}`.\n- The site-review test `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` compares the delivered subject message to the approved template, which is filled with selector-based values.\n- `fn[submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion]` asserts that the submit tool descriptions tell the model to use \"outline selectors, never line numbers\".\n- The citation-review payload (`citations_value`) carries role, name and commentary only. It has no line numbers.\n\n**Other points**\n- The tests that exercise the sanitizer feed it synthetic strings, plus one real parse error. Other parser message shapes, such as a JSON position suffix, fall under the same regex family as the tested YAML and TOML forms. That is not a distinct input class, so I do not count it as a gap.\n- The rejection and resubmission of rationales that cite line numbers belongs to the separate `requirements.authoring.line_numbers.*` requirements, not to this subject.\n- There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
